1
00:00:01,066 --> 00:00:04,096
[Episode 15] Yes, this is Galchi's house.

2
00:00:04,096 --> 00:00:07,156
Galchi, it's Uncle.

3
00:00:07,156 --> 00:00:11,266
Uncle, where are you? Where are you at?

4
00:00:11,266 --> 00:00:14,236
Stand up. We have to hurry and go home.

5
00:00:14,236 --> 00:00:16,196
Somewhere far.

6
00:00:16,196 --> 00:00:17,496
Just some place far.

7
00:00:17,496 --> 00:00:19,241
Mom!

8
00:00:21,526 --> 00:00:27,106
I'm healthy and doing well, so don't worry.

9
00:00:27,106 --> 00:00:30,696
I'm doing very well. I'm calling so you won't worry.

10
00:00:30,696 --> 00:00:32,716
Let's hurry home.

11
00:00:41,946 --> 00:00:43,366
It's Eunchae.

12
00:00:46,716 --> 00:00:50,106
Eunchae is in front of our house, Uncle.

13
00:00:50,916 --> 00:00:52,046
Hi.

14
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:03,536
Where are you going? Where are you going?

15
00:01:13,116 --> 00:01:17,846
Eunchae is still sitting in front of our house, Uncle.

16
00:01:31,436 --> 00:01:33,866
Eunchae.

17
00:01:33,866 --> 00:01:37,186
Is Eunchae still there?

18
00:01:38,936 --> 00:01:41,266
Whoa, it's pretty.

19
00:01:47,576 --> 00:01:51,336
Yes, Eunchae is still here.

20
00:02:36,286 --> 00:02:42,956
Is Eunchae still there?

21
00:02:50,776 --> 00:02:54,726
Is Eunchae still there?

22
00:03:08,456 --> 00:03:17,436
Galchi, is Eunchae still there? She's not leaving?

23
00:03:32,336 --> 00:03:33,706
Eunchae?

24
00:03:57,256 --> 00:04:00,146
What is wrong, Yun? Huh?

25
00:04:00,146 --> 00:04:03,286
Why aren't you taking your shots and medication?

26
00:04:04,486 --> 00:04:06,186
What is wrong, Yun?

27
00:04:14,226 --> 00:04:16,736
Why are you acting like this?

28
00:04:18,866 --> 00:04:23,676
Why are you refusing your shots and medication? Why?

29
00:04:23,676 --> 00:04:26,056
Do you want to die like this?

30
00:04:26,056 --> 00:04:28,126
Do you want to die like this?

31
00:04:31,226 --> 00:04:34,666
Yun, you can't do this.

32
00:04:34,666 --> 00:04:37,266
You can't do this, son. Okay?

33
00:04:37,266 --> 00:04:42,856
I don't know why you are doing this,
but did I do something wrong?

34
00:04:42,856 --> 00:04:45,166
I beg of you.

35
00:04:45,166 --> 00:04:50,026
Please get the shots, and take the medicine.
Please, son?

36
00:04:52,606 --> 00:04:55,706
Do you really want to see your mother die?

37
00:04:55,706 --> 00:04:59,136
Should I just die in front of you? Should I die?

38
00:05:02,506 --> 00:05:07,656
Seriously, what is the problem?
Is it because Muhyeok disappeared? Huh?

39
00:05:07,656 --> 00:05:10,476
What does Muhyeok have anything
to do with you, really?

40
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:13,916
You said you weren't going to take his heart anyway!

41
00:05:13,916 --> 00:05:17,776
In all honesty, whether he lives
or dies has nothing to do with you!

42
00:05:17,776 --> 00:05:19,866
Why do you care so much?

43
00:05:22,376 --> 00:05:23,386
Yun?

44
00:05:24,086 --> 00:05:27,626
Hey, hey!

45
00:05:27,626 --> 00:05:28,766
Yun?

46
00:05:29,406 --> 00:05:32,746
I'm sorry, Yun. Are you okay?

47
00:05:32,746 --> 00:05:35,826
Yun, I beg of you.

48
00:05:35,826 --> 00:05:39,536
Seriously, I'll get down on my knees and beg.

49
00:05:39,536 --> 00:05:43,336
If there's something that I did
wrong, you must forgive me.

50
00:05:43,336 --> 00:05:48,406
From now on, I'll do whatever you ask,
everything you tell me to do.

51
00:05:48,406 --> 00:05:51,906
So let's get the shots, take the pills and live.

52
00:05:51,906 --> 00:05:54,446
Yun, let's live and see what will come next.

53
00:05:55,946 --> 00:05:57,966
Hey, Yun.

54
00:05:59,396 --> 00:06:00,476
Yun?

55
00:06:00,476 --> 00:06:02,746
Nurse? Nurse?

56
00:06:56,306 --> 00:07:03,246
Galchi, is Eunchae still there?

57
00:07:26,086 --> 00:07:31,636
Because Eunchae called so many times,
I have no battery left.

58
00:07:32,936 --> 00:07:36,206
Eunchae must know that you are with me.

59
00:07:37,206 --> 00:07:40,946
I don't think she'd misunderstand or
be sad that you ran away with me.

60
00:07:40,946 --> 00:07:44,266
I think she knows why you left.

61
00:07:46,566 --> 00:07:49,886
You left so it wouldn't be hard on her, right?

62
00:07:53,486 --> 00:07:56,056
How painful.

63
00:07:56,056 --> 00:08:01,216
Your love brings tears to my eyes.

64
00:08:03,696 --> 00:08:12,346
But aren't you punishing me a little too harshly?

65
00:08:14,396 --> 00:08:21,046
Because I took love for granted,
this is the treatment I get?

66
00:08:25,646 --> 00:08:32,006
Galchi, is my Eunchae still there?

67
00:08:43,636 --> 00:08:47,366
Eat this, Eunchae. What if you faint from hunger?

68
00:08:49,866 --> 00:08:53,506
It's okay. I won't faint.

69
00:08:54,536 --> 00:08:59,666
Until uncle comes, I'll be fine.

70
00:08:59,666 --> 00:09:01,146
Don't worry.

71
00:09:11,956 --> 00:09:16,766
Have some porridge. I special-ordered it.

72
00:09:16,766 --> 00:09:20,176
Did you know that you haven't even
had a single sip of water here?

73
00:09:20,176 --> 00:09:24,516
What are you planning to do?
Are you trying to end it all here?

74
00:09:29,856 --> 00:09:32,046
[Song Eunchae]

75
00:09:36,596 --> 00:09:45,516
Galchi, is our stupid Eunchae still there?

76
00:09:46,846 --> 00:09:50,696
May I have a ticket to Seoul?
Whatever flight is next available.

77
00:10:03,606 --> 00:10:08,656
I followed Cha Muhyeok around
because I was interested in him.

78
00:10:08,656 --> 00:10:10,196
That's all.

79
00:10:11,196 --> 00:10:12,846
Minju.

80
00:10:13,666 --> 00:10:19,136
To me, love is just a game. Like Starcraft.

81
00:10:19,136 --> 00:10:21,746
I lost that game.

82
00:10:21,746 --> 00:10:24,166
Cha Muhyeok.

83
00:10:24,166 --> 00:10:26,726
Whether you'll kill him, or save him, he's yours.

84
00:12:44,156 --> 00:12:48,806
How could you come to such a great place without me?

85
00:12:50,726 --> 00:12:54,606
It's not good to be so selfish, Mister.

86
00:13:08,566 --> 00:13:09,946
Mister.

87
00:13:12,806 --> 00:13:14,216
Mister.

88
00:13:15,196 --> 00:13:16,636
Mister.

89
00:13:16,636 --> 00:13:19,666
Go home. Go.

90
00:13:19,666 --> 00:13:20,676
No.

91
00:13:20,676 --> 00:13:23,446
I don't want to see you.

92
00:13:23,446 --> 00:13:28,226
That's why I ran away. Why'd you follow me here?

93
00:13:30,306 --> 00:13:32,666
I don't care what you say. I'm not leaving.

94
00:13:32,666 --> 00:13:34,796
I'm not going to give you up anymore.

95
00:13:35,676 --> 00:13:38,356
Not going, I'm not going.

96
00:13:38,356 --> 00:13:42,156
Go ahead and try. I won't let you out of my sight.

97
00:13:43,256 --> 00:13:44,506
Mister.

98
00:13:46,466 --> 00:13:49,646
Mister. Mister.

99
00:15:16,646 --> 00:15:20,336
I'll take care of Yun, so take her and go home.

100
00:18:19,006 --> 00:18:24,516
Dying isn't such a big deal.

101
00:18:25,796 --> 00:18:28,146
It's a normal part of life.

102
00:18:29,206 --> 00:18:32,846
Everyone dies.

103
00:18:35,196 --> 00:18:38,846
While you're alive,

104
00:18:38,846 --> 00:18:42,096
love like crazy.

105
00:18:42,096 --> 00:18:48,636
Live happily, beautifully, kindly.

106
00:18:48,636 --> 00:18:51,516
That's how to live.

107
00:18:53,086 --> 00:18:57,356
To waste it away like this...

108
00:18:57,356 --> 00:19:00,406
Don't you feel robbed of
the precious time you have left?

109
00:19:00,406 --> 00:19:02,646
Cha Muhyeok, you blockhead.

110
00:19:07,106 --> 00:19:09,796
I know why you keep running from me. You're thinking,

111
00:19:11,996 --> 00:19:16,886
"How sad she'll be, my Blockhead.

112
00:19:18,166 --> 00:19:20,406
It'll be so hard for her."

113
00:19:22,146 --> 00:19:28,006
I know that's why you keep trying to run away.

114
00:19:30,706 --> 00:19:36,136
But, there is something that you don't know.

115
00:19:37,566 --> 00:19:42,706
The ones who get left behind go on no matter what.

116
00:19:45,046 --> 00:19:48,986
It's more sad for the one who is dying.

117
00:19:48,986 --> 00:19:53,486
People who are bound to live
will do anything to do so.

118
00:19:58,286 --> 00:20:01,216
And I'm a blockhead.

119
00:20:02,956 --> 00:20:08,946
I lose things and I forget things easily.
I'm not very smart.

120
00:20:11,946 --> 00:20:20,126
I bet after just a month,
I'll have forgotten all of it.

121
00:20:23,296 --> 00:20:30,026
That one month might be tough,

122
00:20:32,386 --> 00:20:35,376
but after that,

123
00:20:35,376 --> 00:20:42,396
I'll meet my friends and talk. Go out and eat.

124
00:20:42,396 --> 00:20:48,516
Watch funny TV shows and laugh.

125
00:20:48,516 --> 00:20:50,946
I'll be fine again.

126
00:20:54,406 --> 00:20:59,936
So you don't have to worry about me.

127
00:21:06,126 --> 00:21:13,666
The only thing I ask is you don't make me regret.

128
00:21:16,166 --> 00:21:19,016
I don't want to say to myself,

129
00:21:21,146 --> 00:21:23,436
"I wish I'd been kinder to him.

130
00:21:26,336 --> 00:21:30,576
I should have loved him more."

131
00:21:30,576 --> 00:21:32,746
Don't let me regret anything.

132
00:21:37,696 --> 00:21:40,146
Let's have fun, Mister.

133
00:21:44,246 --> 00:21:50,116
Let's not cry. Let's not be sad.

134
00:21:51,646 --> 00:21:58,796
Do your best to happily and joyfully

135
00:21:58,796 --> 00:22:00,646
live with me.

136
00:22:04,816 --> 00:22:08,846
Live with me, Mister.

137
00:22:11,086 --> 00:22:12,676
Okay.

138
00:22:15,716 --> 00:22:17,406
Let's live.

139
00:22:20,936 --> 00:22:22,966
Let's live, Blockhead.

140
00:23:09,482 --> 00:23:11,019
[Pervert]

141
00:23:37,006 --> 00:23:40,536
[Cha Muhyeok, Mister Pervert]

142
00:23:40,536 --> 00:23:43,716
[Song Eunchae the Blockhead]

143
00:24:50,606 --> 00:24:53,776
- Thank you!
- Enjoy!

144
00:24:58,576 --> 00:25:00,136
It looks good, huh?

145
00:25:02,736 --> 00:25:03,946
Here. Ah!

146
00:25:04,556 --> 00:25:05,836
What is it?

147
00:25:05,836 --> 00:25:08,266
Eat it. It's good.

148
00:25:08,266 --> 00:25:10,506
- I don't want it.
- It's good, eat it! Hurry!

149
00:25:10,506 --> 00:25:12,606
Here. Ah!

150
00:25:14,376 --> 00:25:16,116
Good, right?

151
00:25:28,696 --> 00:25:29,596
Why not?

152
00:25:29,596 --> 00:25:33,476
You can't. You're sick.

153
00:25:33,476 --> 00:25:35,436
You're mean.

154
00:25:37,326 --> 00:25:40,326
Instead, eat this. Ah.

155
00:25:40,326 --> 00:25:41,776
Say ah.

156
00:25:43,366 --> 00:25:45,406
Good job.

157
00:25:51,556 --> 00:25:54,556
What is this? Is this for eating, too?

158
00:25:54,556 --> 00:25:55,836
How do you eat this?

159
00:25:55,836 --> 00:25:59,556
Like this.

160
00:26:06,146 --> 00:26:07,526
Like this?

161
00:26:18,382 --> 00:26:24,116
♪ Jingle bells, jingle bells, jingle all the way ♪

162
00:26:24,116 --> 00:26:25,706
Seo-kyeong.

163
00:26:26,906 --> 00:26:29,266
I bought hot buns for you.

164
00:26:29,266 --> 00:26:30,946
Thank you, Grandpa.

165
00:26:30,946 --> 00:26:32,186
Excuse me.

166
00:26:32,186 --> 00:26:37,066
I think I'll be making big bucks soon.

167
00:26:37,066 --> 00:26:39,706
Should I buy you ten truckloads of hot buns?

168
00:26:39,706 --> 00:26:40,776
Really, Grandpa?

169
00:26:40,776 --> 00:26:42,286
Of course!

170
00:26:42,286 --> 00:26:46,006
I'll be making a lot of money
because of you, Seo-kyeong.

171
00:26:50,266 --> 00:26:51,946
Excuse me.

172
00:26:57,016 --> 00:27:00,916
You've been meeting publishing companies, I heard.

173
00:27:00,916 --> 00:27:02,906
News travels fast.

174
00:27:02,906 --> 00:27:07,086
I wrote a book about Audrey.

175
00:27:07,086 --> 00:27:11,856
I've been to several.
I'm looking for the best deal, though.

176
00:27:11,856 --> 00:27:13,246
None of it was Audrey's fault.

177
00:27:14,436 --> 00:27:17,336
It wasn't her doing.

178
00:27:17,336 --> 00:27:23,896
Audrey thinks her children died.
Everything was my doing.

179
00:27:23,896 --> 00:27:26,026
How is that important?

180
00:27:26,026 --> 00:27:26,916
Sir.

181
00:27:26,916 --> 00:27:30,056
Then go tell her now that her children are alive.

182
00:27:30,056 --> 00:27:32,846
Though she'll find out soon enough on her own.

183
00:27:32,846 --> 00:27:33,976
Sir.

184
00:27:33,976 --> 00:27:37,906
I thought this was it for me.

185
00:27:37,906 --> 00:27:41,976
But I think I'll live happily now thanks to you.

186
00:27:41,976 --> 00:27:46,596
I'll be sure to repay my gratitude.

187
00:28:06,656 --> 00:28:08,316
Yun.

188
00:28:08,316 --> 00:28:11,646
Come on. Really, what is wrong with you, Yun?

189
00:28:26,476 --> 00:28:28,576
Is it because of Cha Muhyeok?

190
00:28:29,426 --> 00:28:33,756
Because of him, you're not
taking the shots nor the medicine?

191
00:28:35,086 --> 00:28:38,056
Are you going to die with him?

192
00:28:41,276 --> 00:28:43,196
Is it because you're sorry?

193
00:28:44,376 --> 00:28:47,816
Because you're sorry that your mother left him?

194
00:28:47,816 --> 00:28:51,166
You don't want to go on living selfishly?

195
00:28:51,166 --> 00:28:52,726
Is that why you're doing this?

196
00:28:52,726 --> 00:28:54,456
How did you know?

197
00:28:57,296 --> 00:29:02,236
How did you know Muhyeok is my brother?

198
00:29:26,306 --> 00:29:30,376
No. It's not that song.

199
00:29:30,376 --> 00:29:32,146
Then what could it be?

200
00:29:32,836 --> 00:29:35,796
That also has the word "lay" in it, too.

201
00:29:38,246 --> 00:29:41,316
There is also a song called "Lay By The Ocean."

202
00:29:56,776 --> 00:30:03,256
Beside Mom...

203
00:30:03,256 --> 00:30:05,246
Lay down.

204
00:30:07,456 --> 00:30:09,636
It had the word "mom" in it.

205
00:30:10,586 --> 00:30:12,946
Lay down beside Mom?

206
00:30:15,236 --> 00:30:17,876
Lay down beside Mom.

207
00:30:20,646 --> 00:30:22,676
Oh!

208
00:30:24,586 --> 00:30:38,466
♪ The leaf boat I left is still fresh in my mind ♪

209
00:30:38,466 --> 00:30:49,486
♪ Even as I lay here in my mother's lap ♪

210
00:30:49,486 --> 00:30:55,376
♪ It must still be floating along the pond ♪

211
00:30:57,506 --> 00:31:05,466
♪ Between the blue moon and white clouds ♪

212
00:31:17,726 --> 00:31:21,346
If it hurts, just scream. Let it out.

213
00:31:24,976 --> 00:31:27,026
If it hurts, yell.

214
00:31:29,286 --> 00:31:33,266
Yell out that it hurts.

215
00:31:57,136 --> 00:31:58,786
Are you okay?

216
00:32:01,396 --> 00:32:05,246
Of course I'm okay. Wait out there.

217
00:32:15,616 --> 00:32:18,156
I said I'm fine.

218
00:32:18,156 --> 00:32:21,086
You don't have to look after me like that.

219
00:32:33,696 --> 00:32:35,246
You must've been shocked, right?

220
00:32:40,866 --> 00:32:43,116
Honestly, you were shocked.

221
00:32:44,626 --> 00:32:46,846
Don't remember this.

222
00:32:48,936 --> 00:32:53,946
How I look now. Forget it.

223
00:32:53,946 --> 00:32:55,756
It's embarrassing.

224
00:32:56,816 --> 00:32:59,246
Don't worry.

225
00:32:59,996 --> 00:33:03,206
I'm a pro when it comes to forgetting.

226
00:33:03,206 --> 00:33:08,416
I had a crush on Yun for 20 years but
forgot all of it, just like that.

227
00:33:08,416 --> 00:33:12,286
Don't worry. I'll heroically forget it all for you!

228
00:33:39,656 --> 00:33:41,646
Aren't you coming to bed?

229
00:33:42,676 --> 00:33:46,326
Oh, I will.

230
00:33:48,036 --> 00:33:50,486
You sleep first.

231
00:33:50,486 --> 00:33:54,256
I can't sleep because you're walking around.

232
00:33:58,296 --> 00:33:59,946
Come here.

233
00:34:15,636 --> 00:34:17,386
Are you scared?

234
00:34:20,216 --> 00:34:23,136
You're scared because
I might do something to you, right?

235
00:34:26,056 --> 00:34:29,166
I have some class, you know.

236
00:34:41,336 --> 00:34:43,956
You're going to fall off the bed.

237
00:34:43,956 --> 00:34:46,096
Come closer.

238
00:34:46,966 --> 00:34:50,766
It's okay. I'll just sleep like this.

239
00:34:52,816 --> 00:34:57,726
Why are you so weird?
Are you really my pure-hearted Blockhead?

240
00:34:57,726 --> 00:35:03,146
Then why are you being weird?
Are you really Mister Pervert?

241
00:35:17,776 --> 00:35:20,646
Someone said that

242
00:35:20,646 --> 00:35:26,166
the saddest people in the world are
the ones without fond memories.

243
00:35:27,976 --> 00:35:31,696
It's true. I agree.

244
00:35:33,146 --> 00:35:41,546
I could live all my life
with just one beautiful memory...

245
00:35:47,536 --> 00:35:56,446
With just that memory, I think I would be happy.

246
00:36:32,646 --> 00:36:34,306
Go to sleep.

247
00:36:37,336 --> 00:36:39,736
Pervert.

248
00:36:39,736 --> 00:36:43,946
If you touch me, you're dead.

249
00:37:02,336 --> 00:37:03,896
Fool.

250
00:37:08,916 --> 00:37:10,446
Fool.

251
00:37:53,656 --> 00:37:55,806
Your eyes.

252
00:38:05,706 --> 00:38:07,806
Your lips.

253
00:38:17,476 --> 00:38:18,756
Nose.

254
00:38:23,446 --> 00:38:25,866
Your handsome face.

255
00:38:33,016 --> 00:38:35,116
Ugly face.

256
00:39:50,346 --> 00:39:53,196
I really appreciate it. Thank you, doctor.

257
00:39:58,616 --> 00:40:00,926
Yeah. I heard.

258
00:40:00,926 --> 00:40:06,696
I heard. I heard everything you and Muhyeok said.
I was right by the door.

259
00:40:07,456 --> 00:40:12,006
Your brother must have wanted
to take everything that you had.

260
00:40:12,006 --> 00:40:14,216
The guy in the car that day...

261
00:40:17,616 --> 00:40:19,046
Was that Muhyeok?

262
00:40:39,016 --> 00:40:40,886
Where's my brother?

263
00:40:43,316 --> 00:40:45,046
You know, right?

264
